\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Take-Home Exercise \'97 Tech Lead Hiring\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 TierForge: Resilient Bulk Store Scoring & Tiering\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Context\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 You're building 
\f0\b TierForge
\f1\b0 , a service that ingests a large list of stores, enriches each one with a few business metrics via a slow, rate-limited, and occasionally unreliable API, then scores and tiers every store (Large / Medium / Small) based on user-configurable weights.\
That enrichment API is one we provide and candidates run entirely on their own machine \'97 no internet access, account signup, or API key involved. It's built to 
\f2\i behave
\f1\i0  like a flaky third-party dependency (latency, rate limits, random failures) purely so the resilience problem is real, not to require any actual external integration.\
The interesting part isn't the enrichment metrics themselves (we've synthesized those) \'97 it's building a job engine that reliably processes thousands of records against a flaky external dependency, and a scoring layer that stays fast and re-runnable independent of that slow ingestion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. What We're Evaluating\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Architecture
\f1\b0  \'97 how cleanly the slow, unreliable enrichment step is separated from the fast, deterministic scoring/tiering step.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Resilience
\f1\b0  \'97 how the system behaves under the failure modes described in Section 5 (timeouts, transient errors, a worker going silent, a systemically broken run).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Concurrency correctness
\f1\b0  \'97 safe parallel processing without lost or duplicated work.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Code quality
\f1\b0  \'97 readability, naming, error handling, consistency.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Data modeling
\f1\b0  \'97 how jobs, chunks/units of work, raw enrichment results, and computed scores/tiers are represented in the DB.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Tests
\f1\b0  \'97 unit tests are not mandatory but are a strong positive signal, especially around retry/backoff logic, the scoring formula, and tiering boundaries.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 You're free to use AI tools while building this. The bar is on the output: code you can explain and defend in a follow-up conversation, not just code that compiles.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Time box:
\f1\b0  2\'963 days of effort. See Section 6 for what's in vs. out of scope \'97 this exercise is intentionally meatier than a CRUD app, so scope discipline matters.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Tech Stack\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Frontend:
\f1\b0  React preferred (any modern framework is acceptable).\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Backend:
\f1\b0  Python or Node.js preferred.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Database:
\f1\b0  PostgreSQL preferred (any SQL database is acceptable).\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The enrichment API:
\f1\b0  we provide this (see Section 5) \'97 do not build your own.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4. Functional Flow\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Step 1 \'97 Upload Store List\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 User uploads a CSV of stores (we provide a sample generator and a ready-made file \'97 see Section 5).\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Perform basic header validation before accepting the file, with clear errors on failure.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Columns: store_id, store_name, address, city, state, country.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Step 2 \'97 Run Enrichment Job\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 On submit, a job is created that enriches every store by calling the provided Enrichment API (Section 5), which returns estimated_monthly_footfall, estimated_monthly_revenue, and store_size_sqft per store.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The API is rate-limited and unreliable by design (see Section 5's failure modes) \'97 your job engine has to get all (or as many as possible) stores enriched despite that, without losing track of what succeeded, failed, or is still pending.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Expose a way to see job progress and, for any store that ultimately failed, why.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Example call
\f1\b0  (full contract is in the simulator's own README):\
Request to 
\f3\fs26 POST /enrich
\f1\fs24 :\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 \{\
  "store_id": "ST000001",\
  "store_name": "Fresh Supermarket #1",\
  "address": "71 Church Street",\
  "city": "New Delhi",\
  "state": "Delhi"\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Response:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 \{\
  "store_id": "ST000001",\
  "estimated_monthly_footfall": 18234,\
  "estimated_monthly_revenue": 142033.50,\
  "store_size_sqft": 6210\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Step 3 \'97 Configure Scoring & Tiering\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For each of the three enrichment metrics, the user sets via the UI: a 
\f0\b threshold
\f1\b0  ("bar") \'97 the minimum value that counts as strong for that metric \'97 and a 
\f0\b weight
\f1\b0  (0\'96100%) for how much clearing that bar contributes to the score. Weights should sum to 100%.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The user also sets the score thresholds that separate Large / Medium / Small tiers (e.g. Large \uc0\u8805  70%, Medium \u8805  40%, else Small).\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Submitting this computes, for every successfully enriched store, a score and a tier:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A store's score is the sum of the weights for every metric bar it clears (so it naturally lands between 0% and 100%).\
\ls5\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The tier follows from comparing that score to the tier thresholds.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 This step must not call the Enrichment API again.
\f1\b0  It should run only against data already fetched in Step 2, be fast, and be safely re-runnable any time the user changes bars, weights, or tier thresholds (e.g. to see how the tier breakdown shifts).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

